# The smallest program that shows what the engine is for.
#
# One number goes in. Two branches take it at the same time — nobody
# said they may, they simply have no path between them — and a fourth
# station waits until both have arrived before it runs at all.
#
# That waiting is the whole scheduler. There is no code anywhere that
# says "wait for both": the station has two input ports, so it runs
# when both hold a value, and not before.

station in keep p entry
  out 0 - twice.0
  out 0 - plus.0

station twice double_it p
  out 0 - total.0

station plus add p
  in 1 = 10
  out 0 - total.1

station total add p result
